<ShortAnswer>
  press <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+D</kbd> (<kbd>⌘+Shift+D</kbd> on a Mac) and Chrome bookmarks every tab in
  the window into one new folder. To keep them with notes, find one later and have them on your
  other computers, save them to a board in a tab manager such as TabCabin.
</ShortAnswer>

<h2>1. Bookmark every tab at once</h2>
<p>Chrome can put all the tabs of a window into one bookmarks folder.</p>
<ol>
  <li>
    Press <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+D</kbd>, or open the ⋮ menu → Bookmarks and lists → Bookmark all tabs.
  </li>
  <li>Name the folder, for example with today's date, and press Save.</li>
  <li>
    To get them back, right-click the folder in the bookmarks bar or the bookmark manager and choose
    Open all.
  </li>
</ol>
<p>
  Good for a quick backup before you close a window. Less good for finding one tab later: a folder
  of forty titles has no notes and no order.
</p>

<h2>2. Save a tab group</h2>
<p>
  Tab groups keep related tabs together in the tab strip. Right-click the group's name and save it:
  Chrome keeps the group after you close it, and you can open it again from the bookmarks bar.
</p>
<p>
  Good for a few groups you reopen often. A saved group lives only in Chrome and is still a row of
  tabs, with no notes or to-dos.
</p>

<h2>3. Let Chrome reopen them after a restart</h2>
<p>
  In Settings → On start-up, choose Continue where you left off, and Chrome opens your last windows
  when it starts. <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+T</kbd> brings back the tab or window you closed last, and History
  → Recently closed shows the rest.
</p>
<p>The tabs stay open, though, which is where we started.</p>

<h2>4. Save them to a board with TabCabin</h2>
<p>
  TabCabin is a free, open-source extension that turns the new tab page into boards of tabs, links,
  notes and to-dos. Saved tabs become cards you can drag into groups, find with search and close
  without a second thought.
</p>
<ol>
  <li>Get TabCabin for Chrome, Edge or Brave and open a new tab.</li>
  <li>
    In the tabs panel on the left, open Save all tabs and choose Save all into a new group, or into
    a group you already have.
  </li>
  <li>
    To clear a whole window, choose Save as one group and close. The tabs become one group, “Window
    from” and the date, and the window closes.
  </li>
  <li>
    For one page, <kbd>Ctrl+Shift+S</kbd> saves it with a note and <kbd>Alt+Shift+S</kbd> puts it in
    the Inbox to sort later.
  </li>
</ol>
