<h2>Questions</h2>
<h3>Can I save the tabs of every window at once?</h3>
<p>
  Bookmark all tabs saves the window you are in. In TabCabin the tabs panel lists every window, so
  you can save each one as its own group.
</p>
<h3>Do saved tabs still use memory?</h3>
<p>No. A bookmark or a card on a board is only an address, so closing the tab frees its memory.</p>
<h3>Can I bring my tabs over from OneTab or Toby?</h3>
<p>
  Yes. TabCabin imports OneTab lists, Toby exports and bookmark files from any browser. Step by
  step: moving from <a href="/alternatives/onetab/#moving">OneTab</a> and from{' '}
  <a href="/alternatives/toby/#moving">Toby</a>.
</p>
